const PRIVACY = "This Privacy Policy explains how Jan Seifert (“we”, “us”, “our”), the operator of the SYNTX mobile application (“App”), handles information when you use its AI creation tools, Syntx AI Helper, device features and subscriptions. It also explains your privacy choices and rights.\n\n## 1. Who is responsible for the App\n\nJan Seifert, Camphausenstraße 12, 45147 Essen, Germany, is the operator of the App and the contact for privacy requests. You can reach us at jancao@seifertapp.click. The App does not require account registration, a login or an email address to use its features.\n\n## 2. Information used for AI generation\n\nWhen you request an image or video, the App processes the text prompt, generation options (such as output type and dimensions), and any reference image you choose to provide. The data needed to perform that request is transmitted to fal.ai, which provides AI processing. The generated result is returned to the App.\n\nProviding a reference image is optional. You may choose an image from your photo library or capture one with your camera. The App does not send an existing video file as generation input. Content submitted to an external AI service may be handled by that provider under its own privacy terms and retention practices.\n\n## 3. Syntx AI Helper\n\nSyntx AI Helper is a subscription-based text assistant for improving prompts and answering questions about the App. When you send a message, the text you enter and preceding text messages in that conversation are transmitted to fal.ai to provide a relevant answer. This feature does not accept image, video or other file attachments.\n\nThe App stores your assistant conversation history locally on your device so that it can be displayed and used as context in later requests. We do not maintain our own remote database of that conversation history.\n\n## 4. Camera, photos, microphone and speech\n\nIf you grant access, the App uses the camera to capture reference photos, reads photos you select for AI requests and saves finished images or videos to your photo library. You can choose whether to use these functions and change permissions in your device settings.\n\nFor voice dictation, the App uses the microphone and Apple Speech Recognition to convert speech into a text prompt. The App does not save a separate audio recording and does not transmit audio to fal.ai. Speech recognition can occur on the device where supported, but Apple may process speech data on its servers depending on the language, device and service availability. Such processing is subject to Apple’s applicable privacy practices.\n\nOnly the resulting transcribed text is used for an AI request if you choose to submit it. You can instead enter prompts by typing and decline microphone or speech access.\n\n## 5. Local storage and History\n\nGenerated images and videos, generation history and Syntx AI Helper conversation history are stored locally in the App. The App does not operate a remote content library or a user-account database. Available in-App controls and your device settings allow you to manage content and permissions.\n\nUninstalling the App generally removes its locally stored data, although copies that you saved or shared and any device or operating-system backups may remain. Local storage in the App does not prevent an external provider from processing or retaining the content submitted to that provider to fulfill a request.\n\n## 6. Exporting and sharing content\n\nYou may choose to download generated files or share them through other apps and services. We do not automatically publish your creations or make your history visible to other users. If you share a file, it may be copied, stored or processed by the recipient or destination service under their own terms and privacy policies.\n\nConsider whether a generated image or video contains personal information, or the likeness of another person, before distributing it. Copies you have shared or saved outside the App are not removed merely because you delete the App or clear its local history.\n\n## 7. Subscriptions and related information\n\nSubscriptions are purchased through Apple In-App Purchases. Apple manages payment and billing information. The App uses Apphud to check subscription status and enable premium features; Apphud may process purchase or transaction records, entitlement status and limited app-related identifiers or technical information needed for this purpose.\n\nWe do not collect your payment-card details through the App. You can manage subscriptions and billing through your Apple account. Subscription-related data handled by Apple and Apphud is also governed by their respective privacy documentation.\n\n## 8. Service providers and disclosures\n\nWe use fal.ai to fulfill AI requests, Apple for App Store services and optional speech recognition, and Apphud to support subscription verification. Limited technical routing infrastructure may be involved in enabling AI requests; it is not used by us to maintain a database of your generated content or conversations.\n\nThese services may process information required to deliver, secure and maintain their functions. Their own policies and contractual obligations govern their respective handling of information. We do not sell personal data, operate advertising networks, display advertisements, or use third-party analytics or crash-reporting services in the App.\n\nWe may disclose information if required by law or to protect legal rights, subject to applicable legal safeguards. The App does not offer public profiles, social posting or user-to-user messaging.\n\n## 9. Purposes and legal grounds\n\nWe handle information to provide the image/video creation and assistant functions you request, support local history and export, enable optional device features, validate paid access, operate the service securely and comply with legal obligations.\n\nWhere the General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) applies, processing necessary to provide the functions and paid access requested by you is generally based on performance of a contract. We may rely on legal obligations for required records, legitimate interests for proportionate service security and operation, or consent when the law requires it. Operating-system permissions are separate choices that you can change at any time.\n\n## 10. Retention and international processing\n\nInformation stored by the App remains on your device until you remove it through available controls or uninstall the App, subject to saved exports and backups. We do not set a universal retention period for fal.ai, Apple or Apphud; their own retention rules and legal obligations may apply to information handled by those providers.\n\nDepending on service-provider infrastructure, some information may be processed outside Germany or the European Economic Area. Where applicable law requires international transfer protections, such processing must use an appropriate legal basis and safeguards.\n\n## 11. Your choices and privacy rights\n\nYou can decide whether to submit reference images, use microphone dictation or export and share generated content. You can modify camera, photo, microphone and speech permissions through your device settings. You can use available App controls to manage local history and manage subscriptions through Apple.\n\nDepending on your location and the law that applies, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data, restrict or object to certain processing, request portability where applicable, and withdraw consent when processing relies on consent. You may also lodge a complaint with a competent data-protection supervisory authority.\n\nFor requests relating to data for which we are responsible, email jancao@seifertapp.click. Information processed by Apple, fal.ai or Apphud in their own capacity may also require a request directly to that provider. We will respond to requests as required by applicable law.\n\n## 12. Security and children\n\nWe apply reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the information handled by the App. However, no online service or data transfer is completely risk-free. Protect access to your device and use care when submitting personal information or images of other people.\n\nThe App is not intended to be used in violation of applicable child-protection or privacy laws. Minors should use it only where permitted by local law and, where required, with parental or guardian authorization. We do not knowingly operate a user-account system to solicit personal information from children.\n\n## 13. Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may revise this Privacy Policy as the App’s features, providers or legal requirements change. Where required, we will inform users of material changes. The effective date at the top shows when this version takes effect.\n\n## Contact information\n\nOperator and contact for legal or privacy enquiries: Jan Seifert, Camphausenstraße 12, 45147 Essen, Germany. Email: jancao@seifertapp.click.";

const TERMS = "These Terms of Use (“Terms”) govern the use of the SYNTX mobile application (“App”), offered by Jan Seifert (“we”, “us”, “our”). Please read them before using the App. By using the App, you agree to these Terms, without prejudice to rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law.\n\n## 1. What the App provides\n\nSYNTX allows you to create AI-generated images and videos from text prompts, optionally include reference images, select available models and output settings, and save, review or share the resulting content. The App also includes a text-based Syntx AI Helper feature for improving prompts and answering questions about using the App.\n\nSome functions, including Syntx AI Helper, are available only with an active subscription. Features, generation models, supported formats, usage limits and availability may differ by plan or change over time. AI results are probabilistic and may not match your instructions exactly.\n\n## 2. Eligibility and access\n\nYou may use the App only if you are legally permitted to do so. If you are a minor, any consent required by applicable law must be provided by a parent or legal guardian. You must comply with applicable App Store requirements and local laws.\n\nThe App does not require registration or a separate SYNTX account. Certain paid features are unlocked by a valid App Store subscription.\n\n## 3. Acceptable use\n\nYou are responsible for the prompts, images and instructions you submit and for how you use generated results. You may not use the App to violate the law or the rights of others, including intellectual property, privacy, publicity or data-protection rights; to create or distribute illegal, exploitative, abusive or deceptive content; or to impersonate or misrepresent other people unlawfully.\n\nYou must not attempt to interfere with the App, circumvent subscription controls, access services without authorization, exploit technical vulnerabilities, or disrupt connected systems. We may reasonably restrict misuse where necessary to protect users, third parties and the service, in accordance with applicable law.\n\n## 4. Your inputs and AI-generated content\n\nYou retain any rights you have in the prompts, reference images and other material you provide. You confirm that you have the permissions needed to submit that material for processing. To complete your requests, you authorize the processing of submitted content by the App and the providers used to deliver its functions.\n\nWe do not claim ownership of your input or generated results solely because you use the App. However, laws governing AI-generated works differ, and we do not guarantee that output is unique, copyright-protected, accurate, suitable for commercial use, or free from third-party claims. Similar results may be produced for other users. Review and, where necessary, verify any output before using, publishing or selling it.\n\nWhen you choose to export or share an image or video, the recipient or destination service may process the shared content under its own terms and policies. You are responsible for obtaining any permissions required for distribution.\n\n## 5. Syntx AI Helper\n\nSyntx AI Helper is intended to help you draft and refine prompts and understand App functions. It provides automated text responses, not professional advice. Its responses may be incomplete or mistaken and should be checked before you rely on them. The feature is available to eligible subscribers and is not designed for file uploads or communication between users.\n\n## 6. Paid subscriptions and billing\n\nPaid access is offered through Apple In-App Purchases. The purchase screen presents the applicable price, renewal period and any trial or introductory offer before you confirm payment. Where indicated as auto-renewing, a subscription renews for successive periods unless you cancel it in time through your Apple account settings.\n\nYou can manage or cancel your subscription in your Apple account under Subscriptions. Deleting the App does not cancel an active subscription. Cancellation generally prevents future renewal, while access to paid features ordinarily continues until the end of the current paid period, subject to the subscription terms shown by Apple.\n\nApple processes payments and handles applicable refunds under its policies and mandatory consumer-protection rules. Apphud is used to help verify subscription entitlement inside the App. Nothing in these Terms limits statutory cancellation, refund or other consumer rights that apply to you.\n\n## 7. Intellectual property and brand use\n\nThe App, including its software, interface, design and original text, is protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the App for its intended purposes while you comply with these Terms. This does not grant a right to copy, resell, reverse engineer where prohibited by law, or separately license the App or its elements.\n\nThe SYNTX name and related brand elements are used pursuant to authorization from the rights holder. Ownership of the SYNTX trademarks remains with the applicable rights holder. Your use of the App does not grant independent rights in those marks.\n\n## 8. Third-party services\n\nAI creation and assistant features rely on fal.ai. Device functions, speech recognition and purchases may involve services provided by Apple, and Apphud supports subscription management. These services may have their own applicable terms and privacy practices. Information about processing of personal data is described in our Privacy Policy.\n\nWe are not responsible for content or service terms published by third parties, except to the extent responsibility cannot be excluded under applicable law.\n\n## 9. Availability, updates and service changes\n\nWe aim to provide a reliable service, but individual generation models and other connected functions may be unavailable, delayed or limited because of maintenance, network conditions, demand or provider changes. We may update the App, address security issues, improve features or change available models and capabilities. Where required, we will notify you of material changes affecting paid functionality and respect applicable consumer remedies.\n\nYou may stop using the App at any time. We may suspend access where reasonably necessary to address serious misuse, legal requirements or security concerns, subject to applicable rights.\n\n## 10. Local files and backups\n\nYour generation history, saved creations and assistant conversations are stored locally in the App rather than in an account-based online library. You are responsible for keeping copies of any creations you want to retain. Content may become unavailable if you delete the App, reset or replace your device, or remove local data, unless you have separately exported or backed it up.\n\nSaving or sharing a result through another app or service is a separate action that you control. We cannot retrieve files deleted from your device or guarantee recovery of local history. See the Privacy Policy for more information about storage and the processing of requests by service providers.\n\n## 11. Disclaimers and responsibility\n\nThe App is a creative tool. AI outputs are not verified statements of fact or professional advice. We do not promise a specific result, originality or uninterrupted operation. Any warranties or limitations apply only to the extent permitted by law.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes liability for intentional misconduct, gross negligence, injury to life, body or health, or any other liability that cannot legally be excluded. Mandatory rights of consumers, including rights related to digital services and paid subscriptions, remain unaffected.\n\n## 12. Changes to these Terms and applicable law\n\nWe may update these Terms when necessary to reflect changes in the App, services or legal requirements. We will provide notice of material changes where required. The effective date above identifies this version.\n\nThese Terms are governed by German law, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections afforded by the law of their habitual residence. Disputes may be brought before courts having jurisdiction under applicable law.\n\n## Contact information\n\nOperator and contact for legal or privacy enquiries: Jan Seifert, Camphausenstraße 12, 45147 Essen, Germany. Email: jancao@seifertapp.click.";

